// Single source of truth generating GDScriptFunction::Opcode and encoding per-opcode
// instruction widths, operand kinds, jump targets, fixup references, and variable-width
// relational formulas.
//
// Includers must define:
//   GDSCRIPT_OPCODE_FIXED(m_name, m_word_count, m_operands)
//   GDSCRIPT_OPCODE_VARARG(m_name, m_trailing_words, m_count_tail_offset, m_count_multiplier, m_count_addend, m_trailing_operands)
//
// For fixed opcodes, `m_word_count` includes the opcode word at offset 0 and `m_operands`
// lists the `(m_word_count - 1)` operand kinds at offsets `1 .. m_word_count - 1`.
//
// For variable-width opcodes, `code[ip + 1]` holds `instr_arg_count`, followed by
// `instr_arg_count` packed Address words, followed by `m_trailing_words` trailing operands
// starting at `tail = ip + 2 + instr_arg_count`, satisfying:
//   count = code[tail + m_count_tail_offset]
//   count >= 0 && instr_arg_count == count * m_count_multiplier + m_count_addend

